  "description": "Shenora's Windows shell: application bootstrapper with global exception handling, DPI-correct window-state persistence, single-instance guard with activate broadcast, secondary windows on their own STA threads, tray icon, frameless-chrome form, and the Windows implementations of the Shenora.Core shell contracts (STA file dialogs, clipboard, shell launching, UI-thread dispatcher). Hosts WebView2: environment prewarm, dev-server vs packaged-frontend loading, navigation/new-window/download/permission/process-failure handling, drag-drop zones, and the postMessage IPC bridge with batched event push. Includes auxiliary browser sessions — off-screen driveable sessions with a bounded pool, interactive sessions over an isolated persistent profile, and streaming sessions (CDP screencast out, synthetic input in). Mechanisms only: the kit ships no workflow.",
